---

This section collects practical recommendations for using NAHPU effectively and responsibly before, during, and after fieldwork. Use it as a short field-readiness checklist; detailed procedures remain in the linked canonical guides.

{% aside type="note" title="We would love to hear from you" %}

If you find an effective way to use NAHPU in the field or discover other tips for digital field tools, please [share them with us](https://github.com/hhandika/nahpu/issues).

{% /aside %}

## Explore the recommendations

- [App Setup](./app-setup) — configure NAHPU, prepare projects, and rehearse a catalog session before departure.
- [Project Management](./project-management) — establish identifiers, field and lab workflows, backups, transfers, and export names.
- [Device Care](./device-care) — keep field devices clean, charged, connected only when needed, and ready for GPS work.

Field teams should also consult specimen-care guidance from the [Society for the Preservation of Natural History Collections (SPNHC)](https://spnhc.org/category/wiki/best-practices/) and the [Canadian Conservation Institute](https://www.canada.ca/en/conservation-institute/services/conservation-preservation-publications/canadian-conservation-institute-notes.html).
